WEBVTT

00:00:28.079 --> 00:00:31.663
When you experience something,
like dialing a phone number,

00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:34.829
the experience is converted
into a pulse of electrical energy

00:00:34.871 --> 00:00:38.204
that zips along a network of neurons.

00:00:41.412 --> 00:00:44.746
Information first lands
in short term memory,

00:00:44.787 --> 00:00:47.287
where it's available
from anywhere from a few seconds

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:48.454
to a couple of minutes.

00:00:48.496 --> 00:00:52.287
It’s then transferred to long-term memory
through areas such as the hippocampus

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:55.662
and finally, to several storage
regions across the brain.

00:00:55.704 --> 00:01:00.162
Neurons in the brain communicate 
at dedicated sites called “synapses”